# share

## share > cli
- label: share --help documents all flags, both targets, and shows examples
  command: node ./bin/tracequest.js share --help 2>&1 | grep -q -- '--force'
  tags: [share, share-cli, spec, implemented]

# cli
- label: the CLI selects behavior by first-position subcommands rather than flat mode flags; top-level --list, --latest, and --serve are rejected as unknown options
  command: node ./bin/tracequest.js --help | grep -q 'tracequest <command>' && for opt in --list --latest --serve; do node ./bin/tracequest.js "$opt" >/tmp/tracequest-cli-baseline.out 2>&1; test "$?" -ne 0
  tags: [cli-baseline, implemented]
- label: built-in presets are listed by tracequest presets or tracequest preset; --preset <name> is an option on render, latest, and serve rather than a top-level flat mode
  command: node ./bin/tracequest.js presets | grep -q 'Built-in presets' && node ./bin/tracequest.js preset | grep -q 'Built-in presets' && node ./bin/tracequest.js --help | grep -q -- '--preset <name>'
  tags: [cli-baseline, implemented]
- label: CLI global help, no-args help, help subcommand, and --version finish without importing command implementations or starting live-reload watchers
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/bin/tracequest-startup.test.js
  tags: [spec, cli-startup, implemented]

## search
- label: tracequest search --format handoff writes discovery and indexing progress to stderr so stdout contains only the Markdown handoff
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern handoff test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, cli-search, handoff, implemented]
- label: tracequest handoff <query> directly emits the non-LLM Markdown search handoff, keeping Markdown on stdout and discovery/indexing progress on stderr
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'direct handoff command' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, cli-search, handoff, implemented]
- label: tracequest help and CLI reference document tracequest handoff as the direct Markdown handoff entry point alongside search --format handoff
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'handoff command discoverability|CLI reference and help standup/handoff examples parse' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js test/bin/tracequest-doc-examples.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, cli-search, handoff, docs, implemented]
- label: tracequest handoff <query> accepts --filter <expr> and applies the existing session filter expression before local search/indexing, keeping Markdown on stdout and progress on stderr
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'direct handoff command applies --filter before search' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, handoff, cli-search, implemented]
- label: tracequest handoff <query> accepts --sort recent or --sort date to order matching Markdown handoff results by session mtime after local search matching, while the default remains relevance order
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'direct handoff command orders matching results by recency when --sort recent' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, handoff, cli-search, implemented]
- label: tracequest's synthetic standup/handoff smoke exercises tracequest handoff <query> with --filter and --sort recent against fixture sessions, asserting filtered and recency-ordered Markdown results stay on stdout without invoking prompt agents
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 npm run smoke:standup-handoff
  tags: [spec, handoff, smoke, release, implemented]
- label: CLI reference, help, and CHANGELOG tell users that tracequest handoff --sort recent or --sort date keeps returned quoted-phrase matches exact but may omit older phrase matches beyond the bounded phrase scan cap
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-name-pattern 'handoff quoted phrase sort tradeoff is documented' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, handoff, docs, release, implemented]
- label: tracequest search <query> accepts --sort only for handoff Markdown, and search --format handoff accepts --filter <expr> plus --sort recent|date at the real bin boundary to match the direct tracequest handoff option surface while staying local/non-LLM
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-name-pattern 'search --format handoff accepts direct handoff filter and sort options|search --sort without handoff reports handoff-only usage|handoff command discoverability' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, handoff, cli-search, compatibility, implemented]
- label: tracequest's synthetic standup/handoff smoke exercises legacy search --format handoff with --sort date, proving the documented date alias stays Markdown-only on stdout and does not invoke prompt-agent detection or probes
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 npm run smoke:standup-handoff && TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-name-pattern 'standup/handoff maintainer verification script is documented and wired|handoff command discoverability appears in help and README' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, handoff, smoke, release, compatibility, implemented]
- label: tracequest search and tracequest handoff keep what the near-words re-rank finds in each session file (how many runs of query words together count, the query words of each counted run in the order they appear, whether the session searched for the query) in a near/ folder of the cache directory, one file per set of looked-for words and byte patterns, each entry stamped with the session file's size, modification time and inode; a later search with the same words scores an unchanged session from that cache without reading the file, giving exactly (bit for bit) the score the uncached scan of 29b56c6 gives, also when the word weights differ, while a session file that changed is scanned again and scored as the uncached scan scores its new content; Claude, Codex (its injected lines still ignored) and Grok-format sessions are cached, OpenCode and dsh sessions are always scanned, and TRACEQUEST_NEAR_CACHE=0 turns the cache off
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'near-words cache scores' test/bin/near-cache.test.js
  tags: [spec, cli-search, handoff, search-perf, implemented]
- label: re-scoring six two-megabyte sessions for a repeated query from the near-words cache takes under a tenth of the time of scanning them
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'near-words cache is fast' test/bin/near-cache.test.js
  tags: [spec, cli-search, search-perf, implemented]
- label: a Codex session's function_call_output and custom_tool_call_output text is part of its search terms in both the Node indexer and the sidecar (the whole output up to 2000 chars, else its first and last 1000 chars), so tracequest search '"<phrase>"' finds a Codex session whose phrase occurs only in a tool output, and its first snippet contains the phrase
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'codex tool output phrase' test/bin/codex-tool-output-search.test.js
  tags: [spec, cli-search, codex, implemented]
- label: the snippets of a search made only of quoted phrases are occurrences of those phrases, never matches of a phrase's separate words
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'phrase-only snippets' test/bin/codex-tool-output-search.test.js
  tags: [spec, cli-search, implemented]
- label: a search.idx written before Codex tool output was indexed (format 3) is discarded on load, so already-indexed Codex sessions are re-tokenized and a phrase from their tool output is found without deleting the cache
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'search.idx from before codex tool output' test/bin/codex-tool-output-search.test.js
  tags: [spec, cli-search, codex, implemented]
- label: tracequest search and tracequest handoff rank a session where the query's words appear together (each at most 24 characters from the next) above sessions that only contain the same words far apart, even when the far-apart sessions score higher on word frequency alone, including a long session that word frequency ranks below more than 150 short matches; sessions that only repeat the whole query word for word, in any case or punctuation (a recorded search for it, "Codex Stop-button"), count such copies once, so they do not outrank the session where its words sit together in their own forms, and words that sit together only in Codex's own injected instructions do not count; a session that ran a search or handoff for the query itself keeps half its score; the query's three rarest words are always looked for together, even when one of them is in most sessions; a search with a quoted phrase keeps word-frequency order so its exact matches are never crowded out
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'words together outrank scattered words' test/bin/tracequest-search-ranking.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, cli-search, handoff, search-ranking, implemented]
- label: When run inside a git repository (named by its origin remote and by its folder, so a worktree in a differently named folder still counts), tracequest search and tracequest handoff rank sessions whose project is named after that repository, or that name the repository at least 20 times (a session run in a worktree folder), above otherwise equal matches from other projects; run outside a repository, the same query keeps its original order
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'current repository project ranks first' test/bin/tracequest-search-ranking.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, cli-search, handoff, search-ranking, implemented]
- label: a tracequest search or handoff with --filter leaves index.json and search.idx holding every discovered session, so the next unfiltered search re-indexes nothing, while the filtered results are still ranked with the word statistics (session count, word document counts, average length, vocabulary) of the filtered sessions alone
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'filtered search keeps the full index' test/bin/search-startup-perf.test.js
  tags: [cli-search, search-perf, implemented]
- label: the sidecar scan remembers each Codex session's project in scan-meta.json in the tracequest cache dir, keyed by file path, size and mtime, so a repeat scan reads no unchanged Codex file, a file whose size or mtime changed is read again, and the scan output is the same with and without the cache
  command: cd sidecar && cargo test -q scan_meta_cache && cd .. && TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'scan meta cache' test/bin/search-startup-perf.test.js
  tags: [cli-search, search-perf, implemented]
- label: tracequest search and tracequest handoff without --filter load only the search command's modules: the HTML renderer, the server, share, standup, import and usage-limit modules are not loaded
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'search loads only search modules' test/bin/search-startup-perf.test.js
  tags: [cli-search, search-perf, implemented]
- the sidecar scan stats only directory entries whose file name marks a session file (rollout-*.jsonl, chat_history.jsonl, *.jsonl), not every file inside a Grok, vktr, Codex, Claude, Cursor or Factory session directory @search-perf @implemented
- label: tracequest search and tracequest handoff build a result's snippets for all of its matched words in one pass over the session: each line's command, file-path and error fields are found, decoded and lowercased once and then tested against every word, and the snippets (text, type, order, per-word limit, stop when the first word has its snippets) are exactly the ones the per-word scan of 29b56c6 gives, for claude- and grok-format sessions, whether the lines come from the file or from the in-process line cache, including words that only match after lowercasing a Kelvin sign or a dotted capital I, fields decoded from \u escapes, and overlapping field keys
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'one-pass snippets match per-word scans' test/bin/snippet-scan-one-pass.test.js
  tags: [spec, cli-search, handoff, search-perf, implemented]
- label: scanning one multi-megabyte session for the snippets of six words takes less than three times as long as scanning it for one word (the per-word scan of 29b56c6 took more than four times as long)
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'one-pass snippet scan cost' test/bin/snippet-scan-one-pass.test.js
  tags: [spec, cli-search, search-perf, implemented]
- label: The combined search speed branches preserve the existing search and handoff ranking, exact result replay and cache invalidation behavior in the integration tests
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/bin/tracequest-search-ranking.e2e.test.js test/bin/near-cache.test.js test/bin/search-result-cache.test.js
  tags: [spec, search-speed-integration, implemented]
- label: tracequest search and tracequest handoff without --filter remember their ranked results (with snippets) in search-results.json in the tracequest cache dir, keyed on the exact query, limit, format, sort and current repository plus a fingerprint of every discovered session (path, size, mtime, source, project), the size, mtime and inode of index.json and search.idx, the TRACEQUEST_* environment and the tracequest code files; an exact repeat with that whole key unchanged prints the remembered results without loading the index or reading session files, and its stdout and stderr are byte-identical to the run that computed them
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'result cache repeat' test/bin/search-result-cache.test.js
  tags: [spec, cli-search, handoff, search-perf, implemented]
- label: the search result cache only stores results from a run that left index.json and search.idx untouched, and a session whose file changed (size or mtime), a new or removed session, another query, limit, format, sort or repository, or a rewritten index misses the cache, so the next search prints what an uncached search prints; --filter searches, TRACEQUEST_VERBOSE=1 and TRACEQUEST_NO_RESULT_CACHE=1 never use it
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'result cache invalidation' test/bin/search-result-cache.test.js
  tags: [spec, cli-search, handoff, search-perf, implemented]

## standup
- label: tracequest standup help and CLI reference examples show prompt-agent configuration and --print-input auditing before LLM execution
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-name-pattern 'standup help documents selection windows and env defaults|CLI reference documents standup windows' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, implemented]
- label: tracequest standup accepts --agent-timeout-ms and fails with a clear timeout error when the prompt agent exceeds the configured deadline
  command: node --test --test-name-pattern 'agent timeout|--agent-timeout-ms' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, implemented]
- label: tracequest standup streams prompt-agent stdout and stderr as they are produced while still capturing both streams for timeout and failure diagnostics
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'runPromptAgent streams stdout and stderr|standup streams configured agent output|cmdStandup formats agent failures' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, implemented]
- label: tracequest standup --profile <name> loads standup defaults from HOME/.tracequest/standup-profiles.json and lets explicit CLI flags override profile values
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'standup profiles' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, profile, implemented]
- label: tracequest standup --profile <name> keeps --print-input as an audit-only path that prints compact standup input without invoking any profile-configured agent
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'standup profile print-input audit' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, profile, implemented]
- label: tracequest standup help and CLI reference document --profile, the HOME/.tracequest/standup-profiles.json location, and supported profile keys
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-name-pattern 'standup profile docs' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, profile, implemented]
- label: tracequest standup --workday selects sessions modified during the current local 09:00-17:00 workday window by discovery mtime before compact input, and it is mutually exclusive with --since, --today, and --yesterday
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'workday' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, workday, implemented]
- label: tracequest standup profiles may set workday as the selection-window default, explicit CLI selection-window flags override profile workday, and help plus CLI reference document the key
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-name-pattern 'workday|standup profile docs|standup help documents' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, profile, workday, implemented]
- label: tracequest standup help and CLI reference distinguish built-in detected prompt agents from configurable custom agents, document Droid detection, and tell users to verify or wrap non-stdin agents before using --agent-command
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-name-pattern 'standup (help|CLI reference).*prompt agents' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, agent, docs, implemented]
- label: tracequest standup --dry-run-agent-detection reports the resolved prompt-agent command from CLI/env/profile/default detection without discovering sessions, building compact input, invoking an agent, or sending a prompt
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'standup dry-run agent detection' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, agent, dry-run, implemented]
- label: tracequest standup help and CLI reference document --dry-run-agent-detection as a JSON audit mode that skips session discovery, compact-input building, agent invocation, and prompt sending
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-name-pattern 'standup help documents selection windows|CLI reference documents standup windows' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, docs, dry-run, implemented]
- label: tracequest documents optional installed Claude and Droid standup prompt-agent smoke steps that use only synthetic compact input, record local skip/pass findings, and require wrappers for custom agents that do not read stdin directly
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-name-pattern 'installed prompt-agent smoke guide' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, agent, smoke, docs, implemented]
- label: tracequest standup --probe-agents probes built-in installed prompt-agent candidates with synthetic prompts only, exits before profile loading, session discovery, real-trace compact input building, or private prompt sending, and reports passed, failed, missing, and skipped agents
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'standup --probe-agents' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, agent, probe, implemented]
- label: tracequest help, CLI reference, and package scripts document the opt-in standup agent probe as synthetic-only and separate from normal standup execution
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-name-pattern 'standup probe docs|standup --help includes probe|npm probe:standup-agents' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, agent, probe, docs, implemented]
- label: tracequest standup without --print-input resolves the prompt-agent after candidate session discovery but before expression indexing, session parsing, or compact-input building, so missing-agent failures do not read private trace content or expose parse paths
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'standup missing agent is reported before selected sessions are parsed' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, privacy, implemented]
- label: tracequest standup help and CLI reference use matching audit-mode privacy wording for --dry-run-agent-detection and --probe-agents, including that dry-run sends no prompt and probe sends no private prompt data
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-name-pattern 'standup audit-mode privacy docs' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, docs, privacy, dry-run, probe, implemented]
- label: tracequest CLI reference and help standup/handoff examples are exercised through the real bin parser against synthetic sessions and fake prompt agents, so documented commands stay parser-valid without touching private trace data or real agents
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 npm run smoke:standup-handoff-examples
  tags: [spec, standup, handoff, docs, examples, implemented]
- label: bin-level standup and handoff tests share synthetic HOME and fake prompt-agent fixtures while still executing real bin/tracequest.js coverage for broad e2e and documented examples
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'standup --probe-agents|README and help standup/handoff examples parse through the real bin|standup profiles load config through real bin|search --format handoff emits Markdown stdout' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js test/bin/tracequest-doc-examples.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, handoff, test-maintainability, implemented]
- label: tracequest standup --probe-agents exits nonzero when any installed prompt-agent probe fails, while reports containing only missing optional agents still exit successfully with JSON status details
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-name-pattern 'standup --probe-agents exit status reflects failed versus missing probes' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, agent, probe, implemented]
- label: tracequest prompt-agent execution records stdin write errors as controlled failures so an installed probe agent that closes stdin early returns a JSON failed status instead of crashing the CLI with an unhandled EPIPE
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-name-pattern 'standup --probe-agents exit status reflects failed versus missing probes|runPromptAgent reports stdin write errors without unhandled process errors' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, agent, probe, privacy, implemented]
- label: tracequest standup timeout and failure diagnostics keep stdout/stderr snippets bounded while preserving recent tail output from noisy prompt agents
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'timeout diagnostics preserve bounded' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, agent, timeout, cli-robustness, implemented]
- label: CHANGELOG 0.1.2 summarizes the standup and handoff release surface, including non-LLM handoff output, compact standup input privacy, agent audit/probe commands, and synthetic smoke checks
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-name-pattern 'standup and handoff release notes' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, standup, handoff, docs, release, implemented]
- label: tracequest package scripts expose npm run verify:standup-handoff as the maintainer verification command for the standup and handoff release surface, combining serial direct CLI command coverage with synthetic feature and documented-example smoke coverage without requiring real installed prompt agents
  id: mn2
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'standup/handoff maintainer verification script is documented and wired' test/bin/tracequest.e2e.test.js
